WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
A streaming club's members:
January, one thousand.

2
00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:07.490
Then one thousand and ten,
one thousand and twenty,

3
00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:10.270
and in April, one thousand and thirty.

4
00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:13.930
Two newspapers turn the club's
figures into bar charts.

5
00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:17.240
One headline screams: membership soars!

6
00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:20.230
The other shrugs: membership flat.

7
00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:23.800
So how can one soar while
the other stays flat?

8
00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:25.980
Did a paper fiddle the numbers?

9
00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:28.980
In this mission, you'll
read bar charts carefully,

10
00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:31.770
checking what each small square is worth.

11
00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:35.710
You'll draw pie charts, turning
each frequency into an angle.

12
00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.880
And you'll learn to spot
when a chart could fool you.

13
00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:43.650
Your mission: explain how the same
data gave two opposite headlines.
